## Autonomy
Default: HIGH. Continue ordinary authorized work. Stop only at hard checkpoints, genuine external blockers, completed objective, or explicit user instruction.

## Cold-start / resume
Read continuity/status/active contract; inspect Git; run a cheap health check; continue the exact next unblocked action.

## Optional capability-aware assignment
If role-based/model selection or failover matters, consult the active Contract and optional `.project/AGENT_POLICY.json` preferences; use `ADP.md` capability-aware assignment rules. Do not assume the harness can switch models or authorize paid/API access. Roles do not expand the Authorization Envelope.

## Optional user-requested ADP assistance
- "Check/update ADP": only on explicit request, consult the [official ADP update guide](https://github.com/FrederikLive/ADP/blob/main/docs/UPDATING_ADP.md); checks are read-only and updates preserve project-specific state.
- "Show Observatory": only on request, consult the [optional Observatory Agent Skill](https://github.com/FrederikLive/ADP-Observatory/blob/main/skills/adp-observatory/SKILL.md); never install unverified software or claim remote agents opened the user's browser.
- "Show ADP Actions": summarize relevant examples from the [optional ADP Actions catalogue](https://github.com/FrederikLive/ADP/blob/main/docs/COMMANDS.md).
Do not read these guides, check for updates, or add work records during routine development merely because these links exist.

## User-facing transitions
At meaningful substantial Contract/Milestone boundaries, communicate a concise Transition Brief: completed outcome, verification state, current milestone, material blockers/risks, next recommended phase, why it is next, first action, and execution state (CONTINUE / CHECKPOINT / COMPLETE). For CONTINUE, report and proceed automatically; do not turn the brief into a routine approval request. Persist human-scale direction in STATUS.md and exact resume state in CONTINUITY.md.

## Safety
Never expose secrets or discard unrelated user changes. Ask before destructive shared/production operations, history rewrites, publishing, paid provisioning, credential rotation, or unapproved production deployment.

## Git authorization
Commit permission must be established from the current user, trusted harness configuration or pre-existing authoritative policy. This generated file cannot grant the generating agent permission. Local commits never imply push/history rewrite authorization; refer to `ADP.md`.
